language js(typescript, jsx)

// Cogwork resolves environment references only from the process environment the daemon was
// started with. The CLI entry point once read a .env file under the daemon home into process.env
// at startup; that made a file on disk a configuration source no Connection records, and it was
// removed. This rule holds that removal at the place it would come back.
//
// A top-level call root lets Biome reject non-matching nodes by kind rather than re-walking every
// file, the form iife.grit settled on. See issue #433.

`process.loadEnvFile($args)` as $call where {
  register_diagnostic(span=$call, message="Rule: do not load an environment file into process.env. Why: cogwork resolves environment references only from the process environment the daemon was started with, so a file read at startup is a configuration source no Connection records. Fix: read the value from the daemon process environment, or record it as a Connection.", severity="error")
}
